      "message": "I think I\u0027m just interpreting as written that somehow we\u0027re setting the size to 0x80, but we\u0027re actually disabling it.\n\nSee if this matches your meaning:\n\n```\n# When  HW_STACK_PROTECTION is enabled, the NULL pointer exception page size\n# must have size greater or equal ARM_MPU_REGION_MIN_ALIGN_AND_SIZE (0x80).\n# However that MPU configuration prevents access to the NPCX ROM functions at\n# address 0x40-x0x5c. In order to keep HW_STACK_PROTECTION enabled, disable NULL\n# pointer exception handling.\n```",
